Concept Consistency Review — 2025-11-01
---------------------------------------
- *Front matter updates*: Normalised glossary tags and metadata across published concepts:
  - `content/en/concepts/ShuHaRi.md`, `content/en/concepts/chain_of_accountability.md`, `content/en/concepts/circle_of_influence.md`, `content/en/concepts/clean-code.md`, `content/en/concepts/cognitive_biases.md` — aligned tags to glossary entries and, where needed, added summaries plus corrected relationship keys.
  - `content/en/concepts/connascence.md`, `content/en/concepts/dreyfus_model.md`, `content/en/concepts/emotional_communication.md`, `content/en/concepts/helping_attitudes.md`, `content/en/concepts/ikigai.md` — refreshed tag sets, removed duplicate relations, and tidied supporting summaries.
  - `content/en/concepts/leadership-styles.md`, `content/en/concepts/memento_mori.md`, `content/en/concepts/return-on-investment.md`, `content/en/concepts/software_architecture.md`, `content/en/concepts/systems_thinking.md`, `content/en/concepts/testing_pyramid.md` — supplied missing summaries, rebalanced tags, and reinforced architectural context links.
- *Body structure*: Every published concept retains the required Definition → Key Components → Background (Origin/Application/Comparisons) → Examples flow; no section gaps found.
- *Media & shortcodes*: No broken hero images or shortcode assets detected during the pass.
- *Localization*: `content/nl/concepts/` currently lacks translations. Prioritise `content/en/concepts/systems_thinking.md`, `content/en/concepts/software_architecture.md`, and `content/en/concepts/chain_of_accountability.md` for Dutch localisation to cover foundational themes.

Tooling & Automation Ideas
--------------------------
- Add a lint script that parses concept front matter to verify required fields, enforce UUID-in-alias rules, and flag draft placeholders.
- Extend the tag validator used in this pass to run in CI, cross-checking tag names against `data/glossary.toml` for all content types.
- Introduce a shortcode/media checker that resolves `image` references and reports missing assets without requiring manual spot checks.


